Subject: Retire idle Vulkan devices before NVIDIA driver process teardown
Base: llama.cpp a34de8618b25dfc32ee43749db47d767a9f0a25d (b12015)

Why: the pinned backend keeps logical devices through strong buffer-type and
staging references. NVIDIA compiler threads can then race driver exit handlers
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/10528).

Keep registry descriptors stable, retain all external owners, and release idle
logical devices before process exit. A late-registered exit handler also frees
the instance. The additive ggml_backend_vk_cleanup C API refuses live resources
and permits later device recreation; public struct layouts are unchanged.

diff --git a/ggml/include/ggml-vulkan.h b/ggml/include/ggml-vulkan.h
--- a/ggml/include/ggml-vulkan.h
+++ b/ggml/include/ggml-vulkan.h
@@ -24,6 +24,14 @@
 
 GGML_BACKEND_API ggml_backend_reg_t ggml_backend_vk_reg(void);
 
+// Release cached logical devices when no Vulkan backends, buffers, events or pinned allocations remain.
+// Safe to call concurrently with device acquisition/release. Returns false without releasing
+// resources if they are still in use or synchronization fails. Device and buffer-type
+// descriptors remain valid; later operations recreate logical devices. Normal process exit also
+// performs this cleanup, then destroys the VkInstance before the driver's exit handlers run.
+// Releasing the last backend, buffer, event or pinned allocation also attempts device cleanup.
+GGML_BACKEND_API bool ggml_backend_vk_cleanup(void);
+
 #ifdef  __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
